    "visualThesis": "One registered paper-ocean family becomes a miniature cinematic stage through controlled camera language, directional travel, scale changes, and foreground-background crossings.",
    "compositionRules": [
      "Keep the complete yellow submarine as the only hero subject.",
      "The clean rear ocean plate must remain continuous under every camera and layer move.",
      "The foreground seaweed may occlude the submarine but may never supply or erase submarine pixels.",
      "Rear fish remain smaller and quieter than the submarine; foreground fish may cross larger and softer without hiding the hero for more than a brief moment.",
      "All registered members retain one 1024×1024 canvas and top-left origin."
    ],
    "motionLanguage": [
      "Build six readable camera beats inside one uninterrupted underwater scene.",
      "Alternate wide, medium, and close focal framing with visible horizontal tracking and depth parallax.",
      "Reverse the submarine travel vector once, then return to a calm forward drift.",
      "Use separate deterministic rear-fish, front-fish, ambient-bubble, and propeller-bubble fields.",
      "Keep registered-member scale at or above 1 and all relative motion inside the approved reveal envelope."
    ],
    "layerStrategy": "Reuse one reviewed registered 2x2 layer source as a local project source, derive the complete rear, subject, and foreground members deterministically, and add decorative motif fields at independently authored depths."
